message: 'To cite package "slurmR" in publications use:'
type: software
license: MIT
title: 'slurmR: A Lightweight Wrapper for ''Slurm'''
version: 0.5-4
doi: 10.32614/CRAN.package.slurmR
abstract: '''Slurm'', Simple Linux Utility for Resource Management <https://slurm.schedmd.com/>,
  is a popular ''Linux'' based software used to schedule jobs in ''HPC'' (High Performance
  Computing) clusters. This R package provides a specialized lightweight wrapper of
  ''Slurm'' with a syntax similar to that found in the ''parallel'' R package. The
  package also includes a method for creating socket cluster objects spanning multiple
  nodes that can be used with the ''parallel'' package.'
